  (text "GD1\nUCC27524\nSOT-23-5" (at 143 104 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "R4\n10R\ngate" (at 167 110 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "Q1\nIRF9Z34N\nP-ch D2PAK\n18A 55V" (at 191 103 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "D3\nSS310\ncatch\n100V" (at 204 107 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "D4\nMBRS360\nseries\noutput" (at 204 120 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "Q1 P-CHANNEL GATE DRIVE (floating supply):\nGD1 (LM321) powered by floating supply: V+ = WHITE, V- = WHITE - 15V (via ZD1 + R_Z1).\nDAC2 (0-3.3V GND-ref) drives GD1 non-inverting input.\nGD1 output range: (WHITE-15V) to WHITE.\nDAC=4095 (3.3V) -> GD1 output -> WHITE -> Vgs=0V -> Q1 OFF (correct).\nDAC=2480 (~2V) -> GD1 output -> WHITE-13V -> Vgs=-13V -> Q1 max conduction.\nDAC=0 (0V) -> GD1 output -> WHITE-15V -> Vgs=-15V -> Q1 fully enhanced.\nZD1: BZX84C15 SOT-23, cathode=WHITE, anode=GD1 V+.\nR_Z1: 10k 0402 series from WHITE to ZD1 cathode.\nC_Z1: 100nF 0402 decoupling across GD1 supply." (at 15 95 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "TIM3_CH2 NORMAL POLARITY:\nCCR = 0         => output pin LOW  => Vgs negative => Q1 OFF\nCCR = 400(KA_MAX) => PWM 12.5% duty => ~2V effective at 16V rail\nEffective voltage = (CCR / 3200) x V_RAIL\nAdjust KA_MAX via UART: SET KA_MAX <ccr>" (at 15 118 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "D4 MBRS360 — MODE C ESSENTIAL:\nIn mode C, Q1 injects keep-alive while Q2 may simultaneously\ndeadshort the track. D4 blocks reverse current back through Q1.\nWithout D4: Q1 body diode conducts ~46A at 20kHz repetitively.\nIRF9Z34N body diode is not rated for this.\nD4 is the most electrically stressed diode in this design.\nSS34 (3A/80A peak) is marginal. MBRS360 (3A/60V) is specified.\nD4 can be omitted on mode A/B-only boards." (at 15 138 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "D3 SS310 CATCH DIODE:\nConnected across Q1 drain-source.\nProtects against inductive voltage spikes on Q1 turn-off.\n100V rating required on 16V rail — same reasoning as D2." (at 15 165 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))


  (text "FLOATING SUPPLY CIRCUIT:\nZD1 BZX84C15 (SOT-23)\n  Cathode -> WHITE rail\n  Anode -> GD1 V+ pin\nR_Z1 10k 0402\n  WHITE -> ZD1 cathode (current limit)\nC_Z1 100nF 0402\n  Across GD1 supply (ZD1 anode to GD1 V-)\n\nGD1 V- connected to WHITE-15V node (ZD1 anode).\nGD1 V+ connected to WHITE rail.\nDo NOT connect GD1 V- to GND." (at 180 90 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))

